1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,667
A gene appears to be missing.

2
00:00:01,667 --> 00:00:04,392
Is that biology, or a data problem?

3
00:00:04,392 --> 00:00:10,812
GeneTrace investigates genome reliability before researchers build experiments on an uncertain result.

4
00:00:10,812 --> 00:00:14,273
Sequencing produces DNA fragments called reads.

5
00:00:14,273 --> 00:00:19,062
Assembly reconstructs a genome, and annotation marks gene locations.

6
00:00:19,062 --> 00:00:22,300
Think of reconstructing a book and marking its chapters.

7
00:00:22,300 --> 00:00:25,558
A missing chapter label does not prove the text is gone.

8
00:00:25,558 --> 00:00:32,217
Experts need data collection, computational analysis, and biological interpretation together.

9
00:00:32,217 --> 00:00:34,731
Our goal is to automate that investigation.

10
00:00:34,731 --> 00:00:40,194
A rare difference can be natural, so the agent must also know when the cause is unresolved.

11
00:00:40,194 --> 00:00:48,669
We use one hundred quality selected, complete Escherichia coli genomes from NCBI RefSeq, with gene annotations.

12
00:00:48,669 --> 00:00:53,145
MG1655 anchors the comparison panel.

13
00:00:53,145 --> 00:00:59,518
For this demonstration, seven hundred fifty six read pairs were selected from a public Illumina run.

14
00:00:59,518 --> 00:01:04,948
This reference selected subset is not whole run quality control or independent validation.

15
00:01:04,948 --> 00:01:10,765
We select nimT, a gene with frameshift related annotation, and enable fresh analysis.

16
00:01:10,765 --> 00:01:15,109
Meta requests structural annotation inspection, then read alignment.

17
00:01:15,109 --> 00:01:23,255
The application actually executes minimap2 and regional checks on fixed public inputs, and returns newly computed evidence.

18
00:01:23,255 --> 00:01:25,865
The candidate disagrees with selected reads.

19
00:01:25,865 --> 00:01:29,100
That observation exposes a neighboring control tool.

20
00:01:29,100 --> 00:01:32,980
Meta requests it to investigate whether the discrepancy is local.

21
00:01:32,980 --> 00:01:38,363
The application calculates nimR and yeaO from the new alignment, then updates the judgment.

22
00:01:38,363 --> 00:01:42,341
These are executed checks, not just saved result lookups.

23
00:01:42,341 --> 00:01:44,451
The neighboring genes also disagree.

24
00:01:44,451 --> 00:01:49,032
A strictly local assembly error is therefore insufficient as an explanation.

25
00:01:49,032 --> 00:01:58,467
The structured result lists possible biological, assembly, read, or dataset linkage causes, with limitations and next verification.

26
00:01:58,467 --> 00:02:03,977
Exact run to assembly version linkage remains unverified; the cause is unresolved.

27
00:02:03,977 --> 00:02:07,240
We ran the same case with a fixed policy and with Meta.

28
00:02:07,240 --> 00:02:11,026
Both executed four fresh checks and produced equal measurements.

29
00:02:11,026 --> 00:02:15,219
Meta added evidence dependent selection reasons and cited synthesis.

30
00:02:15,219 --> 00:02:22,860
Both share minimum check safeguards, so this single case does not establish improved accuracy or unique AI discovery.

31
00:02:22,860 --> 00:02:26,130
Population context is still a saved analysis.

32
00:02:26,130 --> 00:02:29,379
Fresh execution is enabled for one bounded case.

33
00:02:29,379 --> 00:02:35,273
Commands, versions, hashes, and evidence exports make the investigation reviewable.

34
00:02:35,273 --> 00:02:39,599
This is a working prototype, not a validated diagnostic system.

35
00:02:39,599 --> 00:02:53,973
GeneTrace connects biological context, real analysis execution, and Meta guided interpretation, helping researchers investigate uncertain genome regions before deciding what to trust and what to verify next.
